Looking at this problem, I need to count ordered assignments of weight classes and container counts to three distinguishable drones.

## Setup

Let drone $i$ have weight class $a_i \in \{5, 2, 1\}$ (in units of 10 kg) and container count $n_i \geq 1$. The constraints are:

$$a_1 n_1 + a_2 n_2 + a_3 n_3 = 40$$

and at least one of: $n_3 = n_1 n_2$, $\;n_2 = n_1 n_3$, $\;n_1 = n_2 n_3$.

Define $S_1 = \{n_3 = n_1 n_2\}$, $S_2 = \{n_2 = n_1 n_3\}$, $S_3 = \{n_1 = n_2 n_3\}$. I need $|S_1 \cup S_2 \cup S_3|$.

## Counting $|S_1|$ (where $n_3 = n_1 n_2$)

Substituting: $a_1 n_1 + a_2 n_2 + a_3 n_1 n_2 = 40$. Multiplying through by $a_3$ and factoring:

$$(a_3 n_1 + a_2)(a_3 n_2 + a_1) = 40\,a_3 + a_1 a_2$$

Setting $R = 40a_3 + a_1 a_2$, I need factorizations $R = uv$ with $u \equiv a_2 \pmod{a_3}$, $v \equiv a_1 \pmod{a_3}$, $u \geq a_2 + a_3$, $v \geq a_1 + a_3$.

