## Triple intersection

$S_1 \cap S_2 \cap S_3$ requires $n_1 = n_2 = n_3 = 1$ and $a_1 + a_2 + a_3 = 40$, but $\max(a_1+a_2+a_3) = 15 < 40$. So $|S_1 \cap S_2 \cap S_3| = 0$.

## Final count

$$|S_1 \cup S_2 \cup S_3| = 3 \times 36 - 3 \times 5 + 0 = 108 - 15 = \boxed{93}$$

